<title>USA: Dow fades in final minutes, NYSE lifts curbs.</title>
<headline>Dow fades in final minutes, NYSE lifts curbs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. blue chips retreated again in the final minutes of trade Tuesday, prompting NYSE to lift program trading curbs.</p>
<p>The Dow 30 slipped back to 7308, up 19 points, after a choppy final hour of trading.</p>
<p>The Big Board lifted curbs at 1559 EDT/1959 GMT, one minute before the close.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
